prompt.text:
Repair the source below and return one corrected, complete TypeScript source file with the same exported API.

`renderContactStrip` produces a deterministic HTML fragment. It must return `<nav aria-label="CONTACTS"><h1>TITLE</h1><ul>ITEMS</ul></nav>`, with one item per contact in input order. Each item is `<li><a href="ADDRESS" aria-label="LABEL"><span>GLYPH</span></a></li>`. Escape `&`, `<`, `>`, `"`, and `'` in every inserted value using `&amp;`, `&lt;`, `&gt;`, `&quot;`, and `&#39;` respectively. Reject a blank title and blank label, address, or glyph with `TypeError`. Empty contacts are allowed. Do not mutate the input.

Known-bad source:
```typescript
export interface ContactLink {
  label: string;
  address: string;
  glyph: string;
}

function escapeHtml(value: string): string {
  return value.replace(/[&<>"']/g, character => ({
    "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;", "\"": "&quot;", "'": "&#39;",
  })[character]!);
}

export function renderContactStrip(title: string, contacts: readonly ContactLink[]): string {
  if (!title.trim()) throw new TypeError("blank title");
  const items = contacts.map(contact => {
    if (![contact.label, contact.address, contact.glyph].every(value => value.trim())) {
      throw new TypeError("blank contact field");
    }
    return `<li><a href="${escapeHtml(contact.address)}" aria-label="${contact.label}"><span>${escapeHtml(contact.glyph)}</span></a></li>`;
  }).join("");
  return `<nav aria-label="CONTACTS"><h1>${escapeHtml(title)}</h1><ul>${items}</ul></nav>`;
}
```

